Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 17:41:41 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] tools: the Lath registry, eight tools and no network
 module

Under the lath feature every registry is the Lath one: file_read and file_write, guarded as the full registry guards them, and six host tools (store_get, store_set, solana_slot, solana_fees, solana_balance, lath_verify_chain) as thin clients of one HTTP/1.1 listener on the Unix socket in the new [lath] section, POST /tools/<tool id> with the step's bearer. Descriptions and parameters are the Lath definitions verbatim. assemble skips peripherals, the pipeline, MCP and skills, the run path refuses any other name after assembly, and the tool modules that open a network connection or drive a browser are not compiled. With the feature off only the ignored [lath] section is new.
